ENGLISH 

1. Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains how ZetaWallet (“ZetaWallet”, the “App”, the “Service” or “we”) processes personal data and technical information when users access or use the application.

ZetaWallet is a non-custodial cryptocurrency wallet that allows users to manage digital assets, view information from supported blockchains, send and receive cryptocurrencies and, where available, exchange cryptocurrencies through the third-party service ChangeNOW.

As of the date of this Privacy Policy, ZetaWallet does not provide a direct feature for purchasing cryptocurrencies with fiat currency.

This Privacy Policy should be read together with the ZetaWallet Terms and Conditions.

⸻

2. Data Controller

Controller: Manuel Centrone
Country: Italy
Email: mysecretchatassistenza@gmail.com


For privacy-related requests, users may contact the Controller using the email address above.

⸻

3. Non-Custodial Nature

ZetaWallet is a non-custodial wallet.

ZetaWallet does not act as a custodian of users’ digital assets and does not take possession of users’ funds.

Private keys, seed phrases and other cryptographic credentials used to control digital assets remain under the user’s responsibility according to the technical operation of the App.

The Controller will never ask users to provide their seed phrase or private key through email, customer support or other communication channels.

⸻

4. Information We May Process

Depending on the features used and the technical configuration of the App, we may process:

• public wallet addresses;
• information concerning digital assets;
• blockchain balances;
• transaction hashes;
• transaction information;
• blockchain network information;
• technical information relating to swaps;
• device information;
• App version;
• operating system;
• language and regional settings;
• IP address;
• crash and error information;
• technical information necessary for operation and security.

ZetaWallet does not necessarily require personal identification information for the basic creation and management of a non-custodial wallet, except where such information may be required by specific third-party services.

⸻

5. Blockchain Information

Public wallet addresses and blockchain transactions may be publicly visible.

Blockchain networks are decentralized systems, and information recorded on a blockchain may be permanent and cannot necessarily be modified or deleted by the Controller.

ZetaWallet does not control public blockchains and cannot delete or modify transactions that have already been recorded on a blockchain.

⸻

6. Swaps Through ChangeNOW

ZetaWallet integrates ChangeNOW to provide cryptocurrency-to-cryptocurrency exchange functionality where available.

ChangeNOW may receive technical information required to process a swap request, which may include, depending on the transaction:

• asset being exchanged;
• asset being received;
• amount;
• blockchain network;
• public wallet address;
• destination address;
• transaction information;
• technical information required to execute the swap.

Processing performed by ChangeNOW is subject to ChangeNOW’s own Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.

Users should review ChangeNOW’s official documentation before using the swap functionality.

KYC and AML

ZetaWallet does not directly conduct a KYC process for the basic creation or management of the wallet.

However, this does not mean that swaps performed through ChangeNOW are always exempt from KYC.
ChangeNOW may apply AML/KYC procedures, risk controls, identity verification, geographical restrictions or other requirements depending on the transaction, the user’s jurisdiction and applicable laws.

Users must comply with the procedures and requirements imposed by ChangeNOW when using its services.

⸻

7. No Direct Fiat Cryptocurrency Purchases

As of the date of this Privacy Policy, ZetaWallet does not provide a direct feature for purchasing cryptocurrencies using euros, US dollars or other fiat currencies.

Available exchange functionality concerns swaps between supported digital assets through ChangeNOW and/or other technical infrastructure identified within the App.

⸻

8. Purposes of Processing

Information may be processed to:

1. provide the functionality of the App;
2. display digital assets and blockchain information;
3. enable users to send and receive digital assets;
4. enable available swap functionality;
5. communicate with blockchain providers and technical services;
6. maintain security and prevent abuse;
7. detect errors and technical issues;
8. improve stability and performance;
9. comply with legal obligations;
10. provide customer support;
11. establish, exercise or defend legal claims.

⸻

9. Legal Bases

Where GDPR applies, processing may be based, depending on the specific activity, on:

• performance of a contract or pre-contractual measures;
• compliance with legal obligations;
• legitimate interests of the Controller;
• consent, where required by law.

⸻

